| **`dotenv`** init | Keeps secrets & configurable values out of source code. |
| **Helmet** | Sets a comprehensive set of security‑related HTTP headers. |
| **CORS** | Controls which origins may call the API; using an env‑controlled whitelist is safest. |
| **Rate limiting** | Limits abuse and helps mitigate DoS attacks. |
| **`express.json()` / `express.urlencoded()`** | Normalises request bodies and rejects malformed payloads. |
| **`morgan`** | Logs each request – essential for audit trails & detecting anomalies. |
| **Validation (express‑validator)** | Even if the endpoints currently accept no parameters, validating (or explicitly disallowing) queries protects future modifications. |
| **Explicit `try/catch` + `next(err)`** | Guarantees that any synchronous/async error bubbles to the central handler. |
| **404 handler** | Guarantees a JSON response for unknown routes—no accidental HTML error pages. |
| **Error‑handling middleware** | Centralised response format, hides stack traces in production, logs the error. |
| **Graceful shutdown** | Cleanly closes the listening socket, letting in‑flight requests finish. |
| **Unhandled rejection / exception handlers** | Prevents the process from staying alive in an unknown state. |
| **Port from env** | Allows the app to run on any port (important for cloud platforms). |

